>lev_lex.c:53: previous declaration of `yyoutput'
>lev_lex.c: In function yyunput:

     Use the command
 % touch src/lev_comp.[ly]
and then try again.

     The problem is that after unpacking the source code, the file
src/lev_lex.c ended up with a slightly more recent revision date/time
than the file src/lev_comp.l (and lev_comp.c vs lev_comp.y is subject
to the same situation).  The file src/lev_lex.c is intended for sites
who can't use lex and/or flex, and was created under Ultrix, which uses
slightly different definitions than NeXT.  src/lev_comp.l is the source
file used to generate that file.  'touch'ing will update its time stamp,
which will in turn trigger it to be processed when 'make' is re-run.

